From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dreyk <dreyksmail@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 05:37:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: dma: optional no reread on tx catchup

In mt76_dma_tx_cleanup(), when the descriptor processing loop catches up
to the last read DMA index (q->tail == last), it re-reads the hardware
DMA index register to see if more frames completed while the loop was
running.

On PCIe (MT7612E), this re-read costs ~1350 ns of CPU stall time. In T1
measurements, this accounted for ~28,575 reads (~38.6 ms CPU time) over
30,000 frames. While catching up frees completed frames slightly sooner,
it is not required for correctness because any subsequent completions
will be caught by the next NAPI poll or completion interrupt.

Add a run-time debugfs switch tx_no_reread (/sys/kernel/debug/ieee80211/
phy1/mt76/tx_no_reread, default 0). When enabled, mt76_dma_tx_cleanup()
skips the catch-up re-read. The switch is stored in struct mt76_dev so that
drivers not exposing the switch keep default catch-up behavior.
---
 dma.c             | 2 +-
 mt76.h            | 1 +
 mt76x02_debugfs.c | 1 +
 3 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dma.c b/dma.c
index a67880a9..e804ae3b 100644
--- a/dma.c
+++ b/dma.c
@@ -444,7 +444,7 @@ mt76_dma_tx_cleanup(struct mt76_dev *dev, struct mt76_queue *q, bool flush)
 				mt76_put_txwi(dev, entry.txwi);
 		}
 
-		if (!flush && q->tail == last)
+		if (!flush && !READ_ONCE(dev->tx_no_reread) && q->tail == last)
 			last = mt76_dma_read_dma_idx(q, -1);
 	}
 	spin_unlock_bh(&q->cleanup_lock);
diff --git a/mt76.h b/mt76.h
index 4788af1b..51c980e3 100644
--- a/mt76.h
+++ b/mt76.h
@@ -1049,6 +1049,7 @@ struct mt76_dev {
 	};
 
 	atomic_t bus_hung;
+	bool tx_no_reread;
 };
 
 /* per-phy stats.  */
diff --git a/mt76x02_debugfs.c b/mt76x02_debugfs.c
index 418f331e..c9b68db3 100644
--- a/mt76x02_debugfs.c
+++ b/mt76x02_debugfs.c
@@ -142,6 +142,7 @@ void mt76x02_init_debugfs(struct mt76x02_dev *dev)
 	debugfs_create_u8("temperature", 0400, dir, &dev->cal.temp);
 	debugfs_create_bool("tpc", 0600, dir, &dev->enable_tpc);
 	debugfs_create_bool("tx_skip_idle", 0600, dir, &dev->tx_skip_idle);
+	debugfs_create_bool("tx_no_reread", 0600, dir, &dev->mt76.tx_no_reread);
 
 	debugfs_create_file("edcca", 0600, dir, dev, &fops_edcca);
 	debugfs_create_file("ampdu_stat", 0400, dir, dev, &mt76x02_ampdu_stat_fops);
